{
  "case_id": "2006-05-848",
  "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are there other areas in the law where courts have to take as binding a legal proposition that they think is dead wrong when they --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. HUNGAR",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's quite common. It's quite common, Your Honor, in any regime where review of an agency decision is relegated to the exclusive jurisdiction of one court, as it is here, and enforcement proceedings are brought in a different court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happens if you have a new company that wasn't around when the regulation was issued? Can it -- can it bring a challenge to the conformity of the regulation to the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could it bring it up by a declaration of non-applicability? Could the new company -- how would it --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. HUNGAR",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, it could seek a determination of non-applicability, but -- and it could obtain judicial review of that determination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. HUNGAR",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are several things, Your Honor. First of all the language of the regulation simply does not support that interpretation. What the regulation says is that hours of -- a change in hours of operation is not a physical change."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Alabama and 12 States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the quotation from the amicus brief from the State of Alabama and the 12 States that relied on the Region 4 statement and that's on pages 7 and 8 of that amicus brief"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Phillips, can I ask another sort of basic question? In your view, would it be permissible for the agency to interpret the word -- to adopt a regulatory interpretation of the -- in the PSD regulations of the word \"modification\" that was different from the definition it used under the new source regulations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: No, I think that would be impermissible"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Would it have been permissible for the agency to adopt one definition for 10 years and then change the definition to the other definition for all programs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Yes. I think as long as you maintain consistency between the two, there is a fair amount of discretion for --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0012",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It doesn't produce one more particle per hour, but now we can run it 24 hours a day and previously we'd run it 12 hours a day. So there's going to be twice as much pollution in the air. Now the whole idea of the PSD system is you don't have twice as much pollution in the air, and I guess that's why they wanted to do it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Phillips, I want to be sure I understand your position. Are you saying the statutory text in effect says every regulation using the word modification must employ the same definition, or are you relying on a general principle that when the same word is used it should be used in the same way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: It's a general principle that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: No. It would not be nearly as strong as it is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, could they have said that construction means both modification and then come up with a new word, alteration? Because the statute says the term construction includes modification, so I -- construction can be broader. Could it be an alteration, they would come up with a new term of art, and add that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Absolutely."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c148bc7cb60f4a936abd0ea2f75c723ded54fb9be476b4cf6341319ffc55391d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c148bc7cb60f-0002-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DONAHUE: \"Rate\" is used as an annual rate in 51.166(b) (21) and (b)(23)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-848",
      "confidence": 0.0,
